Subject: [PATCH 15/19] ttf: leave out legacy kern pairs with a mark in them

A shaper applies a kern table ignoring marks, so a pair with a mark in it
never applies. Read as kerning, such a pair made the compiled kern lookup
filter on that mark, and kerning across the mark stopped where the binary
kerned through it.

Assisted by an AI agent (Claude Opus 5.5)
